---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ArticleCTA from '../../components/ArticleCTA.astro';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  '@id': 'https://www.savemygig.com/fix/rekordbox-export-failed#article',
  headline: 'When a rekordbox Export Fails or Lands Corrupt - How to Recover',
  description: 'The export will not finish in rekordbox, or it finished but the CDJ shows nothing? The causes, the quick recovery, and how to make exports bulletproof.',
  author: { '@id': 'https://www.savemygig.com/#org' },
  publisher: { '@id': 'https://www.savemygig.com/#org' },
  datePublished: '2026-07-24',
  dateModified: '2026-07-27',
  inLanguage: 'en',
  mainEntityOfPage: 'https://www.savemygig.com/fix/rekordbox-export-failed',
};
---
<Base
  title="When a rekordbox Export Fails or Lands Corrupt - How to Recover | Save My Gig"
  description="The export will not finish in rekordbox, or it finished but the CDJ shows nothing? The causes, the quick recovery, and how to make exports bulletproof."
  path="/fix/rekordbox-export-failed"
  ogImage="/og/rekordbox-export-failed.png"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" slot="head" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
  <main class="wrap wrap-wide">
    <div class="status-line red">Export_Failed</div>
    <h1 style="margin-bottom:1.5rem">REKORDBOX EXPORT <span class="danger">FAILED</span>?<br />HERE'S THE RECOVERY</h1>

    <div class="panel panel-danger">
      <p style="margin:0"><strong>Short version:</strong> a failed or corrupt export is a database problem, not a music problem. Your tracks are almost always fine, the index the CDJ reads is broken. A clean re-export fixes most cases.</p>
    </div>

        <details class="acc-sec" name="fix-acc">
      <summary><h2 class="acc-h2">The two flavors</h2><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li><strong>Export won't complete:</strong> hangs, errors mid-sync, or rekordbox stops seeing the device. Usually a failing drive, a full drive, or a locked file. If the drive never appears in rekordbox at all, that is a different problem, see <a href="/fix/rekordbox-not-detecting-usb">rekordbox not detecting the USB</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Export "worked" but the player shows nothing / errors:</strong> the database landed corrupt, classic after an unsafe eject. Often shows as <a href="/fix/cdj-error-e-8302">E-8302</a> at the booth.</li>
    </ul>

    
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="acc-sec" name="fix-acc">
      <summary><h2 class="acc-h2">The recovery, in order</h2><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li>Close rekordbox, unplug and replug the USB, reopen rekordbox in <span class="mono">EXPORT</span> mode.</li>
      <li>Check free space, an export onto a nearly-full drive corrupts silently.</li>
      <li>If the device shows in rekordbox: delete tonight's playlists from the device, re-sync them fresh, and eject with the eject button.</li>
      <li>If the device errors or won't sync: copy any music you need off the drive, format it <span class="mono">FAT32</span> + <span class="mono">MBR</span>, and export again to the clean drive.</li>
      <li><strong>Export small.</strong> Tonight's playlists only. A 2,000-track full-library export is where corruption lives.</li>
      <li>Verify: eject, replug, reopen, the device should load with playlists intact before you leave the house.</li>
    </ul>

    
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="acc-sec" name="fix-acc">
      <summary><h2 class="acc-h2">Make exports bulletproof</h2><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li>Always eject from rekordbox, then wait for the OS to release the drive.</li>
      <li>Keep the library healthy: File → Library → Backup Library, monthly.</li>
      <li>Back up the rekordbox library to another drive or cloud.</li>
      <li>Two identical USBs, exported together. The second one is why this article never matters again.</li>
    </ul>
      </div>
    </details>



    <ArticleCTA article="rekordbox_export" />
  </main>
</Base>
